(VAL-11: the same phrase in condition position is a type predicate, not a
 cast — `If numstr is a number then` tests the runtime tag and is false
 while numstr still holds the text "357", so the Otherwise branch fires.
 Position — statement versus condition — is what distinguishes cast from
 predicate.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox VAL-11.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   not num
)
a value called numstr is "357".
if numstr is a number then, print "num".
otherwise, print "not num".
